    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "2b7a9b34",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "2b7a9b34"
      },
      "source": [
        "To get a single **cell**, give `.loc` both the row and the column:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 49,
      "id": "ff09fd58",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.689162Z",
          "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.689114Z",
          "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.690759Z",
          "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.690480Z"
        },
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "ff09fd58",
        "outputId": "dd64353c-73c5-45b0-8315-45ce928953b0"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "np.float64(845.54)"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 49
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "income.loc[90, weekly]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "04ff3f22",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "04ff3f22"
      },
      "source": [
        "So, to recap:\n",
        "\n",
        "- a **row**: `income.loc[90]`, or a range `income.loc[90:95]`\n",
        "- a **column**: `income[\"column name\"]`\n",
        "- a **cell**: `income.loc[90, \"column name\"]`\n",
        "\n",
        "`.iloc[]` does the same by *position* (0, 1, 2, ...) rather than by label; see the [pandas documentation](https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/user_guide/indexing.html).\n",
        "\n",
        "### Exercise\n",
        "\n",
        "How do the equivalised incomes of single adults (`\"Single adult\"`) and childless couples (`\"Childless couple, annual income\"`) compare? Look at the 1st, 50th and 99th percentiles and summarise what this tells you about the value, or price, of coupling."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 50,
      "id": "07a121db",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.691675Z",
