    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "093ff551",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "093ff551"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Filtering by value\n",
        "\n",
        "So far we've selected data by its label. What if we want to filter by **value**? For example, all childless couples with a net equivalised income above £50,000 a year:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 62,
      "id": "c64d5a32",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.958648Z",
          "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.958596Z",
          "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.961152Z",
          "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.960847Z"
        },
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 487
        },
        "id": "c64d5a32",
        "outputId": "ee045d41-24ec-454d-bdd2-76c66dbfc314"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 1000x500 with 1 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "clean[clean[\"Childless couple, annual income\"] > 50000]\n",
        "\n",
        "clean.plot()\n",
        "plt.title(\"A Modest Proposal: the fiscal benefits of coupling\")\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Percentile\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Income per year (GBP)\")\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "bfcff606",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "bfcff606"
      },
      "source": [
        "Let's break this down. The condition inside the brackets gives `True` or `False` for every row:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 63,
      "id": "01592ed9",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
