    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "5a2d5bdd",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "5a2d5bdd"
      },
      "source": [
        "Putting it inside `clean[ ]` keeps only the rows where it is `True`. Other comparison operators:\n",
        "\n",
        "- `==` is equal to (why the double equals?)\n",
        "- `!=` is not equal to\n",
        "- `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`\n",
        "\n",
        "### Exercise\n",
        "\n",
        "On an appropriately labelled graph, plot the incomes of all single adults whose net equivalised income is less than or equal to £10,000 a year. What proportion of the population is this?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "df = clean[clean[\"Single adult\"] <=10000]\n",
        "\n",
        "# index - put in square brackets by first selecting the columns and then the rows\n",
        "\n",
        "# not sure how to plot this without the childless couples showing\n",
        "df.plot()\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Percentile\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Annual income(£)\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Single adults on less than £10000 per year\")\n",
        "plt.show()\n",
        "\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 487
        },
        "id": "wmIaYIZn6sqn",
        "outputId": "49dfe98c-1b78-4df5-de55-49fd5dce4710"
      },
      "id": "wmIaYIZn6sqn",
      "execution_count": 64,
